        "original_id": "101e0793-c918-5f9f-bbeb-08f219e61cc7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan McCafferty, Eddie Vedder, Billy Rankin\n- Bands: Nazareth, Pearl Jam\n- Albums: Rock 'n' Roll Telephone\n- Roles: lead singer, vocalist, guitarist, songwriter\n- Topics: band membership, retirement, album lineup changes, solo career\n\nFacts:\n- Dan McCafferty was born on 14 October 1946 in Dunfermline, Scotland.\n- Dan McCafferty is a Scottish vocalist best known as the lead singer of Nazareth from the band’s founding in 1968 until his retirement from touring in 2013.\n- Billy Rankin is best known for his work with Nazareth from 1980 to 1983 and again from 1990 to 1994.\n- Billy Rankin also had a successful solo career that included the U.S. hit single \"Baby Come Back.\"\n- Eddie Vedder was born as Edward Louis Severson on December 23, 1964.\n- Eddie Vedder is an American musician, singer, and songwriter best known as a member of Pearl Jam, where he performs lead vocals and is one of three guitarists.\n- Rock 'n' Roll Telephone was the last Nazareth album with original singer Dan McCafferty, who left the group before the album’s release.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
